<%# Visual authority: Kurukoo public developer composition — asymmetric reference layout, warm evidence panels, and governance-forward continuation without a separate developer brand. %>
<%- include('_partials/head', { pageStyles: ['/css/kurukoo-public-pages.css?v=6'] }) %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>
<main class="public-composition public-composition--developers container" aria-labelledby="developers-title">
  <section class="public-developer-hero">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Developers</span><h1 id="developers-title">Build around a conversation-first operating system.</h1><p>Kurukoo exposes governed capabilities through canonical conversation, identity, request, provider, agent, connection and evidence boundaries.</p><div class="public-developer-hero__actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/developers/api#api-access">Explore API guidance</a><a class="public-return-link" href="/chat">Start in Web Chat</a></div></div>
    <aside class="public-developer-brief" aria-labelledby="developer-brief-title"><span class="eyebrow">Integration brief</span><h2 id="developer-brief-title">Use the canonical owner, not a shortcut.</h2><dl><div><dt>Conversation</dt><dd>Preserves the user’s context and return path.</dd></div><div><dt>Authorization</dt><dd>Separates eligibility, consent and action.</dd></div><div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Confirms provider, payment or delivery only when observed.</dd></div></dl></aside>
  </section>
  <section class="public-developer-pathways" aria-labelledby="developer-pathways-title"><div class="public-developer-pathways__heading"><span class="eyebrow">Durable product objects</span><h2 id="developer-pathways-title">Compose around what stays true as work moves.</h2><p>Each pathway preserves a distinct product owner while returning people to the same Kurukoo relationship.</p></div><div class="public-developer-pathways__grid"><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#chat"></use></svg><h3>Conversations</h3><p>Create contextual experiences that hand people back to Agent without creating a second conversational identity.</p><a href="/chat">Open Web Chat <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#package"></use></svg><h3>Requests</h3><p>Represent objectives as durable requests with explicit lifecycle, authorization and evidence.</p><a href="/requests">Review request states <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#discover"></use></svg><h3>Capabilities</h3><p>Discover and compose Kurukoo capabilities without bypassing policy or truth boundaries.</p><a href="/capabilities">Explore capabilities <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article><svg class="k-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/icons/kurukoo-icons.svg#channels"></use></svg><h3>Connections</h3><p>Connect channels, devices and external services through one owner-scoped relationship.</p><a href="/connect">Review connections <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div></section>
  <section id="api-access" class="public-developer-governance" aria-labelledby="developer-governance-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">Governance is part of the platform</span><h2 id="developer-governance-title">Powerful integrations keep their boundaries visible.</h2><p>API consumers do not receive a shortcut around authentication, consent, payment, provider verification, execution authorization or evidence. Kurukoo keeps those boundaries canonical so integrations can remain useful without becoming unsafe or misleading.</p></div><div class="public-developer-governance__detail"><strong>Before an integration acts</strong><ul><li>Confirm the current supported capability and access path.</li><li>Keep secrets outside browsers and public source control.</li><li>Reflect pending, unavailable and recovery states as reported.</li></ul><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/api-docs">Read API reference</a></div></section>
</main>
<%- include('_partials/footer') %>
